<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Linux Infrastructure Automation Lab</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --bg: #f6f8fb;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --ink: #1f2937;
      --muted: #586174;
      --line: #dbe2ea;
      --blue: #2563eb;
      --green: #16845d;
      --amber: #9a6700;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      color: var(--ink);
      background:
        linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.09), transparent 38%),
        linear-gradient(315deg, rgba(22, 132, 93, 0.10), transparent 36%),
        var(--bg);
    }

    main {
      width: min(1080px, calc(100% - 32px));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 56px 0;
    }

    .hero {
      display: grid;
      gap: 18px;
      padding: 48px 0 32px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--blue);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1 {
      max-width: 780px;
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem);
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .subtitle {
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .status-bar {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    .pill {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      min-height: 42px;
      padding: 10px 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .dot {
      width: 10px;
      height: 10px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--green);
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }

    .card {
      min-height: 180px;
      padding: 24px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: var(--surface);
      box-shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(31, 41, 55, 0.08);
    }

    .card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .accent-blue {
      border-top: 4px solid var(--blue);
    }

    .accent-green {
      border-top: 4px solid var(--green);
    }

    .accent-amber {
      border-top: 4px solid var(--amber);
    }

    footer {
      margin-top: 32px;
      padding-top: 18px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      main {
        width: min(100% - 24px, 1080px);
        padding: 28px 0;
      }

      .hero {
        padding-top: 24px;
      }

      .grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Deployed automatically with Ansible</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Linux Infrastructure Automation Lab</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        A managed Linux web node configured through repeatable automation,
        service baselines, and security-focused defaults.
      </p>
      <div class="status-bar" aria-label="Managed node status">
        <span class="pill"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Current managed-node hostname: {{ ansible_facts['hostname'] | default('managed-node') }}</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid" aria-label="Automation baseline">
      <article class="card accent-blue">
        <h2>Nginx Web Server</h2>
        <p>Nginx is installed, enabled, and started through an idempotent Ansible playbook.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card accent-green">
        <h2>SSH Hardening</h2>
        <p>Remote administration is protected with a hardened SSH baseline managed as code.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card accent-amber">
        <h2>UFW Firewall Baseline</h2>
        <p>Firewall policy is defined through automation with safe defaults for managed access.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <footer>
      Infrastructure state is managed by Ansible.
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
